      "content": "Consider the following reaction and statements:<br>\n[Co(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>4</sub>Br<sub>2</sub>]<sup>+</sup> + Br<sup>-</sup> <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.181ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -511 1000 522\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> [Co(NH<sub>3</sub>)<sub>3</sub>Br<sub>3</sub>] + NH<sub>3</sub><br>\n(I) Two isomers are produced if the reactant complex ion is a cis-isomer<br>\n(II) Two isomers are produced if the reactant complex ion is a trans-isomer<br>\n(III) Only one isomer is produced if the reactant complex ion is a trans-isomer<br>\n(IV) Only one isomer is produced if the reactant complex ion is a cis – isomer<br>\nThe correct statements are<br> ",
