      "explanation": "When reactant is cis isomer then following reaction takes place. \n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/D8bhReIOwlHBQGQnE/WmvbW3mFV0Wv6WmGNqZvGPRWvaKau/xd2NnHw0G4qJ3LwStQSz14/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 316 English Explanation 1\">\n<br>So, if reactant is cis - isomer then two isomers are produced. \n<br><br>When reactant is trans isomer then following reaction takes place.\n<br><br><img class=\"question-image\" src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/xtn1dotCLezQXOcRe/uMFC7TAI9aO6W3KHhBqZaDcI16ihX/ircXHktQvPDd4dq5eq8F91/image.png\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2018 (Offline) Chemistry - Coordination Compounds Question 316 English Explanation 2\">\n<br><br>So, if the reactant is trans isomer then only one isomer is produced."
